# 5. REGULATORY KNOWLEDGE BASE

This is one of the most important modules.

The Admin must first upload and prepare regulatory documents before AI curriculum generation.

Supported documents:

- UGC regulations and frameworks
- NEP 2020
- National Credit Framework (NCrF)
- National Higher Education Qualifications Framework (NHEQF)
- Applicable university regulations
- Additional approved academic guidelines

FUNCTIONALITIES:

1. Upload PDF and DOCX documents.
2. Select regulatory category.
3. Enter issuing authority.
4. Enter document version.
5. Enter effective date.
6. Extract document text.
7. Extract tables where possible.
8. Split documents into searchable sections.
9. Generate embeddings.
10. Store chunks in pgvector.
11. Extract relevant academic rules.
12. Verify extracted rules through Admin.
13. Maintain document versions.
14. Archive obsolete regulations.

Every regulatory rule must contain:
- Source document.
- Clause or section.
- Page number.
- Document version.
- Effective date.
- Applicability.
- Verification status.

Do not allow unverified or obsolete rules to silently become authoritative generation instructions.

IMPORTANT AI ARCHITECTURE:

Do not assume uploading documents means the AI model has been trained.

Implement RAG to retrieve the appropriate regulatory documents during generation.

Use a separate deterministic rules engine for credit calculations, programme duration, course categories, and other hard academic constraints.

If regulations conflict, flag the conflict for Admin review. Never invent regulatory requirements.

