# 7. AI CURRICULUM GENERATOR

This is the core module of the application.

Admin selects a university and creates a curriculum for a particular programme.

Example:

University: ABC University
Programme: B.E. Computer Science and Engineering
Duration: 4 Years
Semesters: 8
Academic Year: 2027-2028

AI must generate the COMPLETE PROGRAMME CURRICULUM.

The generation process:

STEP 1:
Retrieve the applicable UGC, NEP 2020, NCrF, NHEQF, and university regulations.

STEP 2:
Identify the applicable regulatory requirements.

STEP 3:
Prepare the programme structure.

STEP 4:
Calculate and validate credits using the configured rules engine.

STEP 5:
Generate Programme Outcomes (POs).

STEP 6:
Generate Programme Specific Outcomes (PSOs).

STEP 7:
Generate semester-wise course allocation.

STEP 8:
Generate Course Outcomes (COs).

STEP 9:
Generate unit-wise syllabus for every course.

STEP 10:
Generate course descriptions and learning objectives.

STEP 11:
Generate teaching and learning methods.

STEP 12:
Generate assessment methods.

STEP 13:
Generate learning resources and references.

STEP 14:
Generate CO-PO and CO-PSO mapping.

STEP 15:
Run regulatory and credit validation.

STEP 16:
Show the complete curriculum to Admin for editing and approval.

AI OUTPUT MUST INCLUDE:

- Programme overview
- Programme educational objectives
- Programme outcomes
- Programme-specific outcomes
- Programme structure
- Semester-wise curriculum
- Course categories
- Course codes
- Course titles
- Credits
- Course outcomes
- Unit-wise syllabus
- Teaching methods
- Assessment methods
- Learning resources
- CO-PO mapping
- Credit distribution
- Applicable regulatory references

Generate structured JSON first, validate it, save it to PostgreSQL, and then create Word/PDF documents.

The Admin must be able to:
- Preview generated curriculum.
- Edit any section.
- Regenerate a selected section.
- Save draft.
- Run compliance validation.
- Export Word.
- Export PDF.
- Publish the curriculum.

Do not let AI automatically approve a curriculum or claim regulatory compliance without evidence and validation.

